<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Monroe returns nine days after her first visit, on the morning of her transvaginal ultrasound, and is seen the same day by Dr. Okoye of gynecology. She started the continuous combined pill and naproxen after the first visit and has had no bleeding yet; she had one day of nausea on the pill, which passed. She has not taken diphenhydramine and has slept a little better with the sleep routine. Her gonorrhea and chlamydia tests and urinalysis from the first visit were negative. She has had her first session with the behavioral health clinician. She asks whether she will need an operation, and whether this will stop her from having children. She has had no thoughts of suicide or self-harm. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Treatment</td><td>Continuous combined pill and naproxen for nine days; no bleeding</td></tr><tr><td>Pain</td><td>Pelvic ache on most days, less than before</td></tr><tr><td>First-visit tests</td><td>Gonorrhea, chlamydia and urinalysis negative</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>No diphenhydramine; a little better</td></tr><tr><td>Her questions</td><td>Surgery, and whether she can have children</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.18"/>
    <code code="10187-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Review of systems Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Review of Systems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Result</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Gastrointestinal</td><td>Positive</td><td>One day of nausea on starting the pill; no bowel pain this week</td></tr><tr><td>Genitourinary</td><td>Positive</td><td>Low pelvic ache on most days; no bleeding or urinary symptoms</td></tr><tr><td>Neurological</td><td>Negative</td><td>No headaches or visual aura</td></tr><tr><td>Psychiatric</td><td>Positive</td><td>Still low but hopeful about the plan; no thoughts of suicide or self-harm</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>4 systems reviewed. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

