  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Endometriosis with a left ovarian endometrioma (N80.102)</content>. Transvaginal ultrasound today shows a 3.4 by 2.9 cm cyst in the left ovary with uniform ground-glass contents and no solid parts or internal blood flow, typical of an endometrioma; the left ovary lies against the back of the uterus; the bowel slides freely behind the uterus and no deep nodule of the bowel, rectovaginal septum or bladder is seen; the uterus is normal in size, without signs of adenomyosis; antral follicles 9 on the right and 6 on the left. With her symptoms and examination this establishes endometriosis without surgery. Dr. Okoye advises continuing medical treatment, keeping surgery in reserve, and avoiding repeated ovarian surgery. Anti-Mullerian hormone 2.6 ng/mL, in the typical range for her age. [S]<list><item>Continue the continuous combined pill and naproxen as needed.</item><item>Repeat transvaginal ultrasound in about four months.</item><item>Surgery only if pain does not respond, the cyst grows, or imaging changes.</item><item>Fertility plan: stop the pill when she wants to conceive, after a preconception visit; reproductive endocrinology referral if not pregnant after six months.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Severe painful periods with pelvic pain, suspected endometriosis (N94.6)</content>. Superseded by the diagnosis of endometriosis today. [S]<list><item>Problem resolved.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Major depressive disorder, single episode, moderate (F32.1)</content>. Therapy started. Safety reviewed: no thoughts of suicide or self-harm; the safety plan and the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline are in her phone. [S]<list><item>Weekly cognitive behavioral therapy for the first month.</item><item>PHQ-9 and GAD-7 in about four weeks.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Pelvic pain score (0 to 10), pain with intercourse and bowel movements, and missed working days</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Ache on most days, less than before; no bowel pain this week; no missed work since the first visit</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Bleeding pattern on continuous suppression</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No bleeding in nine days</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Combined pill: adherence, side effects, and reasons to stop estrogen (migraine with aura, high blood pressure, clot symptoms, smoking)</td><td>Every visit, with blood pressure</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Taken daily; one day of nausea; blood pressure 110/70; no migraine with aura, clot symptoms or smoking</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Naproxen: days used each month, and stomach or kidney symptoms</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Naproxen on four days, with food; no stomach pain</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>No opioid, benzodiazepine, or sleep-medicine accumulation; prescription monitoring program</td><td>At the start, then every visit while pain is active</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No opioid or sedative since the first visit; diphenhydramine stopped; the prescription monitoring program was checked at the first visit</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Transvaginal ultrasound: endometrioma size and deep disease</td><td>At diagnosis; repeat at about four months on medical treatment, then yearly or if symptoms change</td><td>Completed today</td><td>3.4 by 2.9 cm typical left endometrioma; no deep nodules; no adenomyosis</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>CA-125</td><td>Not used to diagnose endometriosis</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>The ESHRE guideline advises against CA-125 for diagnosis; the ultrasound features are typical of an endometrioma</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Ovarian reserve (anti-Mullerian hormone)</td><td>For fertility counseling and before any ovarian surgery</td><td>Completed today</td><td>2.6 ng/mL, typical for her age; antral follicles 9 right and 6 left</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Pelvic examination</td><td>At diagnosis, and when pain persists or changes</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Left adnexal and uterosacral tenderness; no rectovaginal nodule</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Surgical evaluation (laparoscopic excision)</td><td>If pain does not respond to medical treatment, the cyst grows, or imaging is atypical</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Discussed by Dr. Okoye; not needed now; kept in reserve</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Pregnancy intention and fertility plan</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Wants a pregnancy in about a year; the fertility plan agreed today</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Depression measure (PHQ-9)</td><td>Monthly during acute treatment, every 2 to 4 weeks in continuation, then periodically</td><td>Up to date</td><td>PHQ-9 12 nine days ago; next in about four weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Anxiety measure (GAD-7)</td><td>At diagnosis and with each depression measure</td><td>Up to date</td><td>GAD-7 8 nine days ago</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Suicide-risk review, safety plan, lethal means, and the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No thoughts of suicide or self-harm; safety plan reviewed; leftover medicines returned to a pharmacy</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Cognitive behavioral therapy engagement</td><td>Weekly for the first month, then every two weeks</td><td>Completed today</td><td>First session done</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Sleep without sedatives</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Regular bedtime; no diphenhydramine</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Worst pelvic pain 3 of 10 or less, and no missed working days for pain, by four months. In progress; target 2026-10-26 [S]</item><item>No opioid, benzodiazepine or sleep-medicine prescription, and naproxen on 10 days a month or fewer. In progress; target 2026-10-26 [S]</item><item>PHQ-9 score below 5 by four months. In progress; target 2026-10-26 [S]</item><item>A written plan for when and how to try for a pregnancy, made with her before the four-month visit. In progress; target 2026-10-26 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Practice Bulletin No. 114: Management of Endometriosis (2010); ESHRE guideline: endometriosis (2022); Chronic Pelvic Pain: ACOG Practice Bulletin, Number 218 (2020); CDC Clinical Practice Guideline for Prescribing Opioids for Pain, United States, 2022 (2022); U.S. Medical Eligibility Criteria for Contraceptive Use, 2024 (2024); U.S. Selected Practice Recommendations for Contraceptive Use, 2024 (2024); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monograph (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Behavioral health weekly. Preventive visit in about eight weeks. Endometriosis review in about three months with the pain score, PHQ-9 and GAD-7, and a repeat ultrasound at about four months. Next scheduled visit 2026-08-17: periodic adult preventive visit with pregnancy planning. [S]</paragraph></text>

